---
import PublicLayout from "../layouts/PublicLayout.astro";
---

<PublicLayout title="DataIO Validate">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-16">
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-500">Validation</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">DataIO Validate</h1>
      <p class="max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-600">
        Validate dataset manifests and tabular or GeoJSON data against the DataIO metadata contract,
        shared type system, and dataset-specific rules using the same core engine across API, CLI, and SDK.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">CLI</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">Run local validation against manifest files and dataset files.</p>
        <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-4 text-sm text-slate-100">dataio validate tabular --manifest manifest.yaml --table table=data.csv</pre>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">SDK</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">Use the same local-first validator directly in Python code.</p>
        <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-4 text-sm text-slate-100">from dataio.sdk.validate import DataIOValidator</pre>
      </section>

      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">API</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-600">Upload a manifest and files to validate through HTTP.</p>
        <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-slate-950 p-4 text-sm text-slate-100">POST /api/v1/validate/tabular</pre>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-slate-900">Admin UI</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-600">
        Administrators can manage the canonical <code>manifest.yaml</code> for a dataset and run
        pre-publication validation for candidate manifest and data files in the web app.
      </p>
      <a
        href="/admin/manifests"
        class="mt-4 inline-flex rounded-full border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900"
      >
        Open Admin Manifest Tools
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Documentation</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-slate-600">
        The manifest contract remains canonical in the docs site. Use it as the normative reference
        for manifest authoring, storage, and validator behavior.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
        <a href="/docs/manifests/" class="rounded-full bg-slate-900 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-white">
          Open Manifest Docs
        </a>
        <a href="/api/v1" class="rounded-full border border-slate-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">
          Open API Docs
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</PublicLayout>
